s typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Each sample contains random </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0" err="1"><a:latin typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>input_ids</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t> and random labels.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Each sample is a fixed-length sequence of 1024 tokens.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>The synthetic vocabulary size is about 50272.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>The synthetic loader pre-generates a cached pool of samples in memory.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>The repeat setting increases dataset length by replaying the same cached samples, not by creating new ones.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>This means the dataset is seen multiple times in one run until the max time or max steps is reached.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" panose="020F0502020204030204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="23" name="Slide Number Placeholder 22"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{4A4EC27F-BFD8-027A-3C6B-4E9D4CAE2935}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldNum" sz="quarter" idx="10"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="10358437" y="457199"/><a:ext cx="1067589" cy="471489"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:fld id="{48F63A3B-78C7-47BE-AE5E-E10140E04643}" type="slidenum"><a:rPr lang="en-US" smtClean="0"/><a:pPr/><a:t>7</a:t></a:fld><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree><p:ext